Error [E2307]: `d` cannot be used directly here without an owning copy
  --> tests/ui/string_view_outlives_owner_explicit.jet:6:12
    |
  6 |     return d
    |            ^
 Why: `d` is a zero-copy view into `email` (`.trim()`/`.after()`/`.before()`); this destination needs an owned `String`, and `copies: .Explicit` keeps the implicit materialization disabled
 Fix: write `~d` first, or remove `copies: .Explicit` to use the default owning copy
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2307
